WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.475
A good gate can be undone
quietly, in four ways.

2
00:00:03.475 --> 00:00:05.481
If your premium licenses lapse,

3
00:00:05.481 --> 00:00:09.725
eligible roles are removed and
expiring grants become permanent.

4
00:00:09.725 --> 00:00:13.448
Whoever can edit Conditional
Access can weaken the gate,

5
00:00:13.448 --> 00:00:18.200
so those roles sit in Tier 0, and policy
changes need a fresh strong sign-in.

6
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:22.155
If approval is on but nobody's
named, the default approvers are the

7
00:00:22.155 --> 00:00:26.550
very admins you made eligible, and
Microsoft documents that as a lockout.

8
00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:31.655
And Microsoft retires the older
PIM interface on October 28,

9
00:00:31.655 --> 00:00:34.412
2026, so old scripts simply break.

10
00:00:34.412 --> 00:00:36.463
The first one is a funding call.

11
00:00:36.463 --> 00:00:39.525
The sponsor and CIO
treat these licenses as

12
00:00:39.525 --> 00:00:42.587
a control dependency,
renewed without a gap.

13
00:00:42.587 --> 00:00:44.420
Next, the one exception.
